Package: mostr
Title: Markov Ordinal State Transition Models
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Johannes", "Schwenke", , "johannes.schwenke@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Felix", "Herkner", , "felix.herkner@meduniwien.ac.at", role = c("aut", "cph")))
Description: Estimate state occupancy probabilities, expected time in
    states and treatment contrasts for longitudinal ordinal outcomes using
    discrete-time Markov transition models, following Rohde et al. (2024)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.10133>. Supports first- and second-order (partial)
    proportional-odds models fitted with 'rms', 'VGAM', or 'rmsb'.
    Confidence intervals come from the delta method, from simulating the
    model coefficients, or from bootstrap resampling of patients. Also
    simulates ordinal trajectories from models based on three clinical
    trials and plots observed and estimated trajectories.
